1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,657
This country had five million people,

2
00:00:02,657 --> 00:00:04,702
its own army and its own khans.

3
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:08,453
In 1876 it was deleted from the

4
00:00:08,453 --> 00:00:08,997
map.

5
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,812
It was the Khanate of Kokand,

6
00:00:11,812 --> 00:00:14,354
founded in 1709 by Shahrukh Biy,

7
00:00:14,354 --> 00:00:16,700
a chief of the Ming tribe of

8
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,045
Uzbeks, in the Fergana Valley.

9
00:00:19,515 --> 00:00:22,114
At its peak it stretched across four

10
00:00:22,114 --> 00:00:24,357
of today's countries: Uzbekistan,

11
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:26,897
Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan and Kazakhstan.

12
00:00:27,117 --> 00:00:28,802
It even ruled Tashkent.

13
00:00:29,272 --> 00:00:31,213
Then the Russian Empire moved south.

14
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:34,868
Tashkent fell in June 1865.

15
00:00:35,088 --> 00:00:38,203
Khujand in 1867.

16
00:00:38,673 --> 00:00:40,643
The last strong khan,

17
00:00:40,643 --> 00:00:43,900
Khudayar, was driven out in 1875 by

18
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,779
revolts against his heavy taxes.

19
00:00:47,249 --> 00:00:50,913
Russian generals Kaufman and Skobelev crushed the

20
00:00:50,913 --> 00:00:53,934
resistance, and in 1876 the khanate was

21
00:00:53,934 --> 00:00:57,340
abolished and turned into the Fergana Oblast.

22
00:00:57,810 --> 00:00:59,635
Today its capital, Kokand,

23
00:00:59,635 --> 00:01:01,401
is a city in Uzbekistan,

24
00:01:01,401 --> 00:01:04,167
and Khudayar Khan's palace is a museum.

25
00:01:04,637 --> 00:01:06,771
Which lost country should I cover next?

26
00:01:06,991 --> 00:01:09,039
Comment below, and follow so you don't

27
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:09,529
miss it.

